 "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nbs -\u003e 63038d535d59\nhsb -\u003e 1f8b62b25065\nit -\u003e a04acf25d7d6\nnl -\u003e 4a05bcabda65\nrm -\u003e a43e8f68c7c3\nsl -\u003e 480c87fa6902\nsq -\u003e ec65836f4de5", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cf9763a759992f70497c0c246961d805203aa152", "parents": ["826b1ba0c55ab55eeb5e1020b549da73464b23ed"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575468028, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "646": {"changesets": [{"author": "Aki Sasaki \u003casasaki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1481916 - add l10n-bumper task. r=Callek,tomprince a=pascal-on-IRC\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D53116", "files": [".cron.yml", "taskcluster/ci/config.yml", "taskcluster/ci/l10n-bump/kind.yml", "taskcluster/docs/kinds.rst", "taskcluster/taskgraph/target_tasks.py", "taskcluster/taskgraph/transforms/release_version_bump.py", "taskcluster/taskgraph/transforms/task.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f5013b2a89492326ea4d67b36b80f2473cac73f5", "parents": ["cf9763a759992f70497c0c246961d805203aa152"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575490035, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "647": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nbs -\u003e 8e54c9338950\nca -\u003e b297019ca631\ncs -\u003e 6bdfa52bf073\nfr -\u003e 48f8f5bfc4a9\nfy-NL -\u003e 2d81dac91c65\ngn -\u003e 4b435b075bc2\nid -\u003e 4269fc07a8c3\nit -\u003e eb460fc72a24\nkab -\u003e cd8e0422c573\nnb-NO -\u003e de741e1a94bc\nrm -\u003e c0c551e2c56b\nsk -\u003e 4672b841f70f\nsq -\u003e 419230385fcd\nuk -\u003e d7698de4bdc1", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9c006434448dc11400f0eb38267988dc303815f2", "parents": ["f5013b2a89492326ea4d67b36b80f2473cac73f5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575554043, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "648": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr68 repo-update HSTS HPKP blocklist remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D55957", "files": ["browser/app/blocklist.xml", "netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/plugins.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5da4320439e3285b06b54e7dff730dfc05810068", "parents": ["9c006434448dc11400f0eb38267988dc303815f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1584391 - Fix intermittent leak in browser_ext_themes_ntp_colors_perwindow.js. r=rpl, a=test-only\n\nFrom extensive testing, it appears that the test fails (also on TV)\nwhen one of the home pages is opened. This did not happen with\n\"about:robots\". Apparently, a browser window leak can be observed if the\ntest starts at a homepage and opens another homepage tab in the test.\n\nThis patch works around the issue by initializing the window with about:blank.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D55108", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_themes_ntp_colors_perwindow.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "73b5825f32b5dd6434e726f9504dcfcd153db15d", "parents": ["5da4320439e3285b06b54e7dff730dfc05810068"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike de Boer \u003cmdeboer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1461242 - Adding a TabState flush would be cheating, so add a wait to allow some time for the cache to be populated. r=dao, a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D46290", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_duplicate_history.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "73c5c3ab1290e192079607a0106e849bde41de86", "parents": ["73b5825f32b5dd6434e726f9504dcfcd153db15d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cphilip.chimento@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1590907 - Determine 64-bit in public JS header without configure macro. r=froydnj,sfink, a=RyanVM\n\nIf only relying on JS_64BIT to determine whether the system is 64-bits,\nthen the result will be incorrect when the header is installed as a\npublic header for use by embedders, and since JS_BITS_PER_WORD affects\nthe layout of structs in header files, things will go badly wrong.\n\nThis uses two other ways of determining pointer width, hopefully\ncross-platform enough. __SIZEOF_POINTER__ is a GCC-ism and probably\nworks in Clang as well. UINTPTR_MAX is hopefully sufficiently\ncross-platform as a last resort.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D52458", "files": ["js/src/jsapi.cpp", "js/src/jstypes.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3d4060cdea6872d53f834ca56a833acf56aa3097", "parents": ["73c5c3ab1290e192079607a0106e849bde41de86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cphilip.chimento@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1590907 - Include JS_FOO macros that influence public API in js-config.h. r=sfink, a=RyanVM\n\nThese are configure macros that start with JS_ and have an effect on the\npublic API declared in JSAPI header files, so they should be included in\nthe installed js-config.h header file.\n\n(Includes ESR68-only JS_UNALIGNED_PRIVATE_VALUES)\n\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1590907", "files": ["js/src/js-config.h.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "11af3f9251b5ed10ce4e94f39d8faa8509e562e7", "parents": ["3d4060cdea6872d53f834ca56a833acf56aa3097"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cphilip.chimento@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1590907 - Revert bug 1553938. r=sfink, a=RyanVM\n\nIt turns out that we don't actually want to install js-confdefs.h\nbecause it contains macro definitions that can conflict when embedders\ninclude JSAPI headers in their Autotools projects.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D52462", "files": ["js/src/build/Makefile.in", "js/src/build/js-config.in", "js/src/build/js.pc.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "085c965a7830ccc60fa6d95cc6739b65a5024936", "parents": ["11af3f9251b5ed10ce4e94f39d8faa8509e562e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeff Walden \u003cjwalden@mit.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1590907 - Use a static assert in HashTable that doesn't depend on configure. r=sfink, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D53921", "files": ["mfbt/HashTable.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f79bfc535dd95f9abcc98d6f4936643a897b4fba", "parents": ["085c965a7830ccc60fa6d95cc6739b65a5024936"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575577629, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "649": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nar -\u003e ba4d9d419260\ncs -\u003e 0d3e29efb564\nfi -\u003e a67ad6810053\nfr -\u003e a72bb6e0fb10\nhu -\u003e f87665372308\nid -\u003e 0e894b5c1f89\nkab -\u003e 518edf7af47c\nnb-NO -\u003e 3548dcc99da6\nnn-NO -\u003e 346b38cfd6e2\nsq -\u003e d861b406abc9\nur -\u003e a0a0a779b363\nvi -\u003e 46d548f25aa6", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "25c6a00611c4d68e0a3711e6a2448af69ef4597a", "parents": ["f79bfc535dd95f9abcc98d6f4936643a897b4fba"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575651426, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "650": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1543156 - Wait for the addon manager to start in DevTools addons xpcshell tests. r=ochameau, a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D52535", "files": ["devtools/server/tests/unit/head_dbg.js", "devtools/server/tests/unit/test_addon_events.js", "devtools/server/tests/unit/test_addon_reload.js", "devtools/server/tests/unit/test_addons_actor.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a2b059948d54076ae53146c1e685489d45735e37", "parents": ["25c6a00611c4d68e0a3711e6a2448af69ef4597a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Perry Jiang \u003cperry@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1540921 - Don't throw when postMessage-ing a closing/closed DedicatedWorker. r=asuth, a=RyanVM\n\nThis behavior is consistent with calling MessagePort.postMessage when the\nentangled port is null.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D55849", "files": ["dom/workers/Worker.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/workers/WorkerGlobalScope-close.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5fe8cdc380b571aac935729578c2cb58f4ec07d0", "parents": ["a2b059948d54076ae53146c1e685489d45735e37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1573360 - Prevent test_ext_downloads_misc.js from failing intermittently due to a missing .part file. r=mixedpuppy, a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D55950", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_downloads_misc.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3c06d0441b70c45777622a4b6762a92ef8d06f0a", "parents": ["5fe8cdc380b571aac935729578c2cb58f4ec07d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1583471 - Update bindgen in ESR68. r=glandium, a=RyanVM\n\nThis allows to build ESR with newer versions of Rust.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D55828", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/bindgen/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/bindgen/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/bitfield_unit.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/helpers.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/features.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/analysis/has_vtable.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/analysis/sizedness.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/comp.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/derive.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/enum_ty.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/function.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/main.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/options.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8506e87cec5078d9ae58f9e6772082382b4c8cc9", "parents": ["3c06d0441b70c45777622a4b6762a92ef8d06f0a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575657554, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "651": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 8506e87cec50 (bug 1583471) for build bustage.", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/bindgen/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/bindgen/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/bitfield_unit.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/helpers.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/features.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/analysis/has_vtable.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/analysis/sizedness.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/comp.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/derive.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/enum_ty.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/function.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/main.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/options.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b9a9e0b6f0df0f9a97d3c64997b68761a51bba22", "parents": ["8506e87cec5078d9ae58f9e6772082382b4c8cc9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575666740, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "652": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nick Thomas \u003cnthomas@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1598436 - add checks for 'latest' bouncer products to cron (beta, deved, release), r=aki a=release DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D54656", "files": ["testing/mozharness/configs/releases/bouncer_firefox_beta.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/releases/bouncer_firefox_devedition.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/releases/bouncer_firefox_release.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "35bc3746ef3588d131b27a5c469b50c8e08fe9d3", "parents": ["b9a9e0b6f0df0f9a97d3c64997b68761a51bba22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nick Thomas \u003cnthomas@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1598436 - add ESR bouncer checks to cron, r=aki a=release DONTBUILD\n\nFixes up ESR bouncer aliases now that ESR60 is EOL.\nAdds check for latest products used by www.mozilla.org.\nEnables the cron checks.\nFixes up a script error which meant we weren't checking all partial platforms in release automation.\n\nDepends on D54656\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D54657", "files": [".cron.yml", "taskcluster/ci/cron-bouncer-check/kind.yml", "taskcluster/ci/release-bouncer-aliases/kind.yml", "testing/mozharness/configs/releases/bouncer_firefox_esr.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/release/bouncer_check.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "15f9e0a61e78b1d2d5bb73e20badb05c39b99d6d", "parents": ["35bc3746ef3588d131b27a5c469b50c8e08fe9d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nick Thomas \u003cnthomas@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1598436 - add nightly bouncer checks to cron, r=aki a=release DONTBUILD\n\nDepends on D54657\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D54658", "files": [".cron.yml", "taskcluster/ci/cron-bouncer-check/kind.yml", "testing/mozharness/configs/releases/bouncer_firefox_nightly.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "16ca1384f658d1518b71ef94052ca2588114e51e", "parents": ["15f9e0a61e78b1d2d5bb73e20badb05c39b99d6d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575849515, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "btara@mozilla.com"}, "653": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr68 repo-update HSTS HPKP blocklist remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D56357", "files": ["browser/app/blocklist.xml", "netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "282e567557533edf4c7d8bc0ec4daae220796f05", "parents": ["16ca1384f658d1518b71ef94052ca2588114e51e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1583471 - Update bindgen in ESR68. r=glandium, a=RyanVM\n\nThis allows to build ESR with newer versions of Rust.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D55828", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/bindgen/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/bindgen/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/bindgen/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/bindgen/csmith-fuzzing/README.md", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/bitfield_unit.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/helpers.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/codegen/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/features.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/analysis/has_vtable.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/analysis/sizedness.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/comp.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/derive.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/enum_ty.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/ir/function.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/main.rs", "third_party/rust/bindgen/src/options.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ad3e56f736525637a5f4db61c57a1ed2a8c026ae", "parents": ["282e567557533edf4c7d8bc0ec4daae220796f05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kirk Steuber \u003cksteuber@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1595470 - Prevent EnsureCorrectPermissions from making faulty assumptions about childBuffer. r=rstrong, a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D52604", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/update/common/commonupdatedir.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a34ba9dd7b822a287e4f0a04da792f35d10be301", "parents": ["ad3e56f736525637a5f4db61c57a1ed2a8c026ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1221256: Implement IAccessible::put_accValue for editable text. r=MarcoZ, a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D53378", "files": ["accessible/ipc/win/handler/AccessibleHandler.cpp", "accessible/windows/msaa/AccessibleWrap.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "27867697bd3cb483f516c618c8f0740f3a1f35d3", "parents": ["a34ba9dd7b822a287e4f0a04da792f35d10be301"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1597792 - Allow clock_nanosleep in the sandbox filter. r=gcp, a=jcristau\n\nIt seems newer glibc versions implement nanosleep() in terms of\nclock_nanosleep(), which broke the profiler due to the sandbox rules\nwhitelisting the former but not the later.\n\nUnfortunate that the profiler will fail in old Firefox versions though... :/\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D53879", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/SandboxFilter.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "37338049043a596d41943a4c21e7277cb3964cca", "parents": ["27867697bd3cb483f516c618c8f0740f3a1f35d3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575918202, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "654": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1598040 - Filter clock IDs in clock_nanosleep sandbox rule. r=gcp a=jcristau\n\nThe `clockid_t` type on Linux has a space of values which encode a pid\nand allow measuring the CPU usage of other processes; we don't want to\nallow sandboxed processes to do that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D54080", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/SandboxFilter.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5c8476f559f61f6380e24f9aa05723821e112ea7", "parents": ["37338049043a596d41943a4c21e7277cb3964cca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Toshihito Kikuchi \u003ctkikuchi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1597963 - Pass VT_ERROR for Explorer to call ShellExecuteExW with null verb. r=aklotz a=pascalc a=jcristau\n\nThe patch for Bug 1588975 specified the \"open\" verb to execute a target, but\nthe default verb is not always \"open\".  For example, the default verb for a font\nfile is \"preview\".  We should specify null verb to start the default operation.\n\nNow we use `IShellDispatch2.ShellExecute` to ask explorer.exe to call\n`ShellExecuteExW`.  That method takes an optional `VARIANT` parameter as a verb.\nAccording to https://devblogs.microsoft.com/oldnewthing/20140919-00/?p=44023,\nwe need to pass `VT_ERROR` to omit an optional parameter.  If we pass\nother values such as `nullptr` with `VT_BSTR` or `VT_EMPTY`, explorer.exe calls\n`ShellExecuteExW` with the empty string `\"\"` instead of `nullptr`, which is not\nconsidered as a valid verb if the target file is not associated with any app.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com//D54603", "files": ["uriloader/exthandler/win/nsMIMEInfoWin.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileWin.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5c45ee1cf34779a351c0caf7b7efc82d6e49872d", "parents": ["5c8476f559f61f6380e24f9aa05723821e112ea7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1560660 - Update mSystemUsesDarkTheme in the child process via caching machinery. r=stransky a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D54199", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsLookAndFeel.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsLookAndFeel.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "befd99804abb8f5343401e1064646d7d2fe91c52", "parents": ["5c45ee1cf34779a351c0caf7b7efc82d6e49872d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575933173, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "nbeleuzu@mozilla.com"}, "655": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1602601 - Add HyperTextAccessible-inl.h include to AccessibleWrap.cpp to fix MinGW build bustage. r=Jamie, a=bustage\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D56481", "files": ["accessible/windows/msaa/AccessibleWrap.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c3d72d38c09e873e0e52a18cb799f55ccf08ebb9", "parents": ["befd99804abb8f5343401e1064646d7d2fe91c52"], "tags": []}], "date": 1575938549, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "656": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nca -\u003e 7c081cb95fda\ncs -\u003e 6712a000c133\nda -\u003e a5925591c8d3\ndsb -\u003e 68aa79ace2ff\neu -\u003e 9380959cce6b\nfr -\u003e 2fd660b5f001\nit -\u003e abb49eef51b7", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"